                <pb facs="0798" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg712"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports that it is authoritatively denied that there is any want
                    or suffering among the Jews in southwestern Russia, and that aid of any kind is
                    unnecessary; that while the offer is appreciated in the spirit in which it was
                    made, it is gratefully declined.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
